      "writtenOn": "2023-07-14T23:02:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Could this be re-structured to be\n\u003e ```\n\u003e if (host_cpu \u003d\u003d \"arm64\") {\n\u003e   # set host_platform to arm64_hermetic\n\u003e } else {\n\u003e   # set host_platform to x64_hermetic\n\u003e }\n\u003e if (target_cpu \u003d\u003d \"arm64\") {\n\u003e   # set platforms and cc_output_directory_tag to mac_arm64_hermetic\n\u003e } else {\n\u003e   # set platforms and cc_output_directory_tag to mac_x64_hermetic\n\u003e }\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e As is, the control flow is a bit tough for me to parse.\n\u003e \n\nDone. I didn\u0027t put in any `else` blocks, instead letting the build figure out what to do with the defaults in the \"not arm64\" case. I think this reads better now that the `cc_output_directory_tag` arguments have been removed.\n\n\u003e The --extra_toolchains should probably go in the .bazelrc file so they are always available (unless this BUILD.gn is not seeing the .bazelrc file, which I would expect to cause other issues).\n\nDone. It looks like moving this to .bazelrc was sufficient, so I removed these lines from here.",
